-- title:
--   Theorem 15: exact energy-conserving universality
-- statement:
--   Let n,d≥1 and ΔE>0, with identical nondegenerate site energies rΔE, 0≤r<d. For every unitary V commuting with their additive intrinsic energy there is W generated by a finite sequence of the G15 controls Z_a, R_{j,a}^{(l)}, and nearest-neighbor R_{j,j+1}^{(l,l')} such that
--
--   $$W(|\psi\rangle|0\rangle_a)=(V|\psi\rangle)|0\rangle_a\quad\text{for all }\psi.$$
--
--   The same W is realizable by finite control pulses in the G17 Hamiltonian, including the intrinsic system and ancilla drift. Real control angles are equivalent to angles in [0,2π) for these integer-spectrum generators. This is exact catalytic implementation without a complexity bound.
-- source:
--   Restrictions on realizable unitary operations imposed by symmetry and locality, arXiv:2003.05524v3, PDF p. 45, Theorem 15: one-ancilla exact energy-conserving universality

import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Papers_Independent_Extend50_P14

noncomputable section

namespace QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Extend50.P14

open scoped Classical Matrix ComplexConjugate Matrix.Norms.Frobenius

open MeasureTheory

-- Exact accepted aliases and physical operators, without local redeclarations.

open QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Information100.P60 (Mat)

open QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Advance50.P49 (onWire multiSwap)

attribute [local instance 100] LieRing.ofAssociativeRing

/-- PDF p.45, Theorem 15/G21: exact finite gates and the drift-containing pulse
model, with one common returned ancilla for every system input. The angles may
be reduced to [0,2π) because each control has integer spectrum. Printed G15 repeats
an ancilla exchange and uses a common j<=n range. Drop the duplicate and use
G10's separate chain/ancilla ranges, since G15 refers to those defined controls. -/
theorem energy_catalytic_universality (n d : ℕ) (hn : 1 ≤ n) (hd : 1 ≤ d)
    (gap : ℝ) (hGap : 0 < gap) (V : EMat n d)
    (hV : V ∈ Matrix.unitaryGroup (EnergyBasis n d) ℂ)
    (hComm : V * intrinsicEnergy n d gap = intrinsicEnergy n d gap * V) :
    ∃ W : Mat (EnergyBasis n d × Bool), W ∈ controlGenerated (energyControls n d) ∧
      HamiltonianLift W V ∧ PulseReachable (energyDrift n d gap) (energyControls n d) W := by sorry

end QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Extend50.P14

end
